","To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the concentration to mg/mL**:  
   The concentration is 0.044% w/v, which means 0.044 g of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution.  
   
   \[
   \text{Concentration} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.0044 \text{ g/mL}
   \]

2. **Convert grams to milligrams**:  
   \( 1 \text{ g} = 1000 \text{ mg} \).  
   \[
   0.044 \text{ g/mL} = 0.044 \times 1000 \text{ mg/mL} = 44 \text{ mg/mL}
   \]

3. **Calculate the mass in 10 mL**:  
   \[
   \text{Mass} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume} = 44 \text{ mg/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 440 \text{ mg}
   \]

Thus, there are \(\boxed{440 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.",fluency,"# Task Description
