","The GELA LNH-93-1 study compared aggressive chemotherapy (ACVBP followed by consolidation) versus standard chemotherapy (CHPO) plus radiotherapy (RT) in patients ≤60 years old with low-risk, stages I–II intermediate-risk non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL). The study demonstrated that **aggressive chemotherapy (ACVBP + consolidation) is superior to standard chemotherapy (CHOP + RT) in terms of progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS) without significantly increasing toxicity.**  

