","To calculate the entropy change (\(\Delta G\)) for the given reaction, we use the formula:
\[ \Delta G = \Delta G_{\text{products}} - \Delta G_{\text{reactants}} \]
where \(\Delta G = \Delta n \times \Delta S\) and \(\Delta S = \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} \).

For the given reaction:
\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g] \]
The molar entropies are:
\[ \text{PbS} = 91.2 \, \text{J/K mol} \]
\[ \text{O}_2 = 205.1 \, \text{J/K mol} \]
\( \text{PbO} = 66.5 \, \text{J/K mol} \)
\[ \text{SO}_2 = 248.2 \, \text{J/K mol} \]

