","The primary structure of a protein is the sequence of its amino acids. It is the simplest aspect of protein structure and serves as the foundation for all other levels of protein folding. The primary structure is defined as the linear chain of amino acids linked by peptide bonds. The sequence is determined by the DNA sequence of the gene that encodes the protein.

