<USER_REQUEST>
A solution has a hydronium ion concentration \([H_3O^+]\) of \(10^{-4}\) M. What is the nature of this solution (acidic, basic, or neutral)?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To determine the nature of the solution, we compare the hydronium ion concentration \([H_3O^+]\) to the concentration of hydroxide ions \([OH^-]\).  

- If \([H_3O^+] > 10^{-4}\) M, the solution is acidic.  
- If \([H_3O^+] < 10^{-4}\) M, the solution is basic.  
- If \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M, the solution is neutral.  

Since the given concentration \([H_3O^+]\) is \(10^{-4}\) M, the solution is neutral.  

Thus, the correct answer is \(\boxed{\text{neutral}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

