\]  
where \(\DeltaS_g\) is the change in density of the gases and \(\DeltaS_w\) is the change in density of the water.  

1. **For the gases**:  
   The heat lost by the gases is:  
   \[
   Q_{g} = m_g \times c \times \DeltaT = m_g \times 1.005 \, \text{kJ/kg K} \times (1100 - 550) \, \circ\text{C} = m_g \times 1.005 \, \text{kJ/kg K} \times 550 \, \text{K} = 55275 \, \text{kJ/kg m}
   \]  
   where \(m_g\) is the mass of the gases.  
   The change in density of the gases is:  
   \[
   \DeltaS_{g} = \frac{Q_g}{T_1} - \frac{Q_g}{T_2} = \frac{m_g \times 1.005 \times 550}{1100} - \frac{m_g \times 1.005 \times 550}{1550} = m_g \times 0.55275 \left(\leftfrac{1}{1100} - \dfrac{1}{1550}\right) = m_g \times 0.55275 \times 0.0004545 = 0.20 \text{ kg/kg m}
   \]  
